{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Collection Item","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404024","type":"Type"}],"id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/library/6729","identified_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"repository number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404621"}],"content":"6729","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"call number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300311706"}],"content":"N70 .M336","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"preferred term","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670"}],"content":"The voices of silence  ","type":"Name"}],"produced_by":{"carried_out_by":[{"_label":"Malraux, André,","id":"actor/malraux-andre","type":"Actor"},{"_label":"Doubleday","id":"actor/doubleday","type":"Actor"}],"timespan":{"_label":"1953","begin_of_the_begin":"1953-01-01T00:00:00Z","end_of_the_end":"1953-01-01T00:00:00Z","type":"TimeSpan"},"type":"Production"},"referred_to_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"inscription statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435414"}],"content":"Accompanied by correspondence between Stephen Porter and Eumie Imm Stroukoff : My parents, Eliot and Aline Porter, were very good friends of Georgia O'Keeffe.  My mother told me a story about her that I've always remembered:  Georgia liked to read in bed, but the book she was reading was too heavy to hold up so she took a bread knife and cut it in half.  The book, The Voices of Silence by Andre Malraux, is that book. -- letter from Stephen Porter, February 9, 2008.|Annotation by unknown on pp. 14-16, 41, 44, 113, 420, 448, 475, 590-593, 595, 598, 600-602, 604-605, 607, 609, 616, 624, 627, 629, 631, 633, 636-637, 639-642.|Book cut in half at p. 272.|Embossed stamp on front loose endpaper : Georgia O'Keeffe / Abiquiu, New Mexico.|grl copy : poor condition ; dust jacket : fair condition ; slipcase : fair condition.","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"description statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"}],"content":"Based on the author's Psychologie de l'art.\nEphemera found between pp. 100-101 : Typed piece of paper : re André Malraux.\nEphemera found between pp. 108-109 : Clipping from unknown source : André Malraux.\nFrom Georgia O'Keeffe's Ghost Ranch library.\nPage marker found between pp. 226-227 and discarded : blank piece of paper with tape.","type":"LinguisticObject"}],"representation":[],"type":"HumanMadeObject"}